{
  "id": "direct-replication",
  "term": "direct replication",
  "definition": "Direct replication is a repeat of an earlier experiment that closely follows the original study design to check whether the same finding appears again. In psychological research, it is used to test the reproducibility of a reported effect, especially when the result is novel or surprising.",
